{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["A prophet from among you, from your brothers, like me — who will command you commandments that are in the Torah, and not like a dreamer of dreams who tells you to worship idols. And what is written: ״וְלֹא קָם נָבִיא עוֹד בְּיִשְׂרָאֵל כְּמֹשֶׁה״ — its meaning is as he explains: ״אֲשֶׁר יְדָעוֹ ה׳ פָּנִים אֵל פָּנִים״; but as for believing the Holy One, blessed be He, he will be like him, and speak truth from Him — and not like a prophet who gives Israel a sign or portent to worship idols."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:39:09.674171557Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}